RF.put("questb:b38",{"8518":{"id":8518,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Linen Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 linen bandages to Sentinel Silversky at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Linen Bandage","desc":"Ever am I amazed by the selflessness exhibited when so many would instead turn to selfishness instead. ‹class›, I am still in need of a number of linen bandages before my assignment here is fulfilled. Will you aid me once more in the collection of those bandages?","rew":"You will receive:\nAlliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Ever am I amazed by the selflessness exhibited when so many would instead turn to selfishness instead. ‹class›, I am still in need of a number of linen bandages before my assignment here is fulfilled. Will you aid me once more in the collection of those bandages?","done":"You are to be commended, ‹name›. While there are those that would take advantage of the economics of our war footing to line their pockets in a fervor of greed, you have proven time and again that your devotion to the Alliance, and indeed to all of Azeroth, comes first.\nBlessings of Elune be with you always!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60,"y":33.3,"n":"Sentinel Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8438":{"id":8438,"t":"Conquering Arathi Basin","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Our conflict with the Alliance has escalated to a true war. No longer are false pretenses to enter into battle used or expected by either side at this point.\nThe battle for the Arathi Basin is one of resources, plain and simple. Either the Alliance gets the resources and uses them against us or we get them and use them to keep our war efforts going. Help the Defilers maintain the flow of resources we need, ‹name›!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with The Defilers","back":"You've come back with news from Arathi, ‹class›?","done":"Securing our resources in Arathi is an important task! You've done well, ‹name›.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"678":{"id":678,"t":"Call to Arms","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Boulderfist Brutes and 4 Boulderfist Magi, and return to Drum Fel in the Hammerfall outpost.\nBoulderfist Brute slain : 0/ 10\nBoulderfist Magus slain : 0/ 4","desc":"Your strength is evident, ‹name›. Now to see how you fare against a real enemy.\nThe Boulderfists have a lair to the southwest of here towards the dwarven bridge, and, if I'm not mistaken, the maulers and magi there shall present to you a greater challenge--they have done so to us thus far.\nSlay as many as you can and come to me in body when you are successful, or come to me in spirit when you fail. I shall give praise to your tenacity in battle either way.","rew":"Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You hesitate. Why? You have shown great strength thus far, ‹name›. Do not fail me now.","done":"You are as strong as a kodo, and your lust for battle does your people proud.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.2,"y":33.9,"n":"Drum Fel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"2758":{"id":2758,"t":"The Origins of Smithing","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,150 experience instead of 4,400, 0.72 times as much.","obj":"Bring six Golden Scale Bracers to Hank the Hammer in Stormwind.\n6 Golden Scale Bracers","desc":"When I was about your age, a dwarf by the name of Galvan took me under his wing and trained me in the ways of the armorsmith. Before he left for Booty Bay, he made me promise to train all those with the desire and determination to advance in the craft of blacksmithing -- so here I am -- all these years later.\nSo, now it's time for you to learn a little something. Make me six golden scale bracers and you will learn where smithing comes from, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Golden Scale Gauntlets\nExperience: 3,150","back":"Could you be the next Galvan protege?","done":"Very good, ‹name›! Listen and learn.\nBlacksmithing never comes from here! <Hank points to his hammer.>\nBlacksmithing never comes from here! <Hank points to the anvil.>\nBlacksmithing only comes from here! <Hank points to his heart.>\nAnd now you know the origin of blacksmithing.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.9,"y":36.8,"n":"Hank the Hammer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97958":{"id":97958,"t":"Camping 101 leatherworking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Shelene Rhobart on the road to Undercity from Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your leatherworking skill to 20","desc":"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, ‹class›. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","done":"There you have it, your very own camp tent. Most folk don't care much for tents being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.4,"y":60,"n":"Shelene Rhobart","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94278":{"id":94278,"t":"Craftsmans writ golden scale gauntlets","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Golden Scale Gauntlets\nGolden Scale Gauntlets","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Golden Scale Gauntlets, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Golden Scale Gauntlets Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94278","cats":["crafting"]},"94358":{"id":94358,"t":"Craftsmans writ shadoweave mask","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Shadoweave Mask\nShadoweave Mask","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Shadoweave Mask, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Shadoweave Mask Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94358","cats":["crafting"]},"2118":{"id":2118,"t":"Plagued Lands","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Capture a living Rabid Thistle Bear and bring it back to Tharnariun.\nShould you fail to capture a Rabid Thistle Bear and lose your trap, return to Tharnariun Treetender and request another trap.\nRabid Thistle Bear Captured\nProvided: Tharnariun's Hope","desc":"A sickness spreads across the Darkshore, gripping the minds and bodies of all it touches.\nThe Thistle Bears have been hit the hardest by this plague. The once noble beasts are now an instrument of destruction - rabid and frenzied. I may have a cure for this ailment.\nTake this trap to the forest and lay it on the ground. Any Rabid Thistle Bear that crosses the light shall become docile for a short time. Once the bear is docile, it shall follow you. Lead it back here, ‹name›.","rew":"Money: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 975\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you brought me the sick animal, ‹name›?\nShould you fail to spring the trap, do not fret - Tharnariun's Hope is eternal. If you require another trap, abandon your task and report back to me.","done":"Our work has only just begun, ‹name›. Are you prepared for your next task?","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.8,"y":43.4,"n":"Tharnariun Treetender","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"2518":{"id":2518,"t":"Tears of the Moon","lv":12,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Priestess A'moora in the Temple of the Moon at Darnassus wants you to bring her Lady Sathrah's Silvery Spinnerets.\nSilvery Spinnerets Lady Sathrah","desc":"Lady Sathrah was once beloved of Elune. Graceful and pure, the spider spun her silver threads through the moonlight, catching the evening mist. The silvery dew had strong healing powers and was kept here in the temple.\nBut of late, Sathrah has descended into madness. Her future generations are now threatened as well.\nFind Lady Sathrah, ‹name›, and end her suffering. She dwells along the northern borders of Teldrassil, near Wellspring Lake. Gather her silvery spinnerets and bring them back to me.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"I regret the task that I have asked you to carry out; but Lady Sathrah is beyond hope.\nIt is our hope to offer the sacrifice of the spinnerets to Elune. With this sacrifice, Elune will bless Sathrah so that she might be reborn, and at peace.","done":"The forest mourns for Lady Sathrah, but it was something that had to be done.\nThank you, ‹name›.\nDarnassus Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":36.7,"y":85.9,"n":"Priestess A'moora","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"7798":{"id":7798,"t":"A Donation of Silk","lv":60,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Silk Cloth Protector Weaver , Mountaineer Langarr 85.7 % , Watcher Wollpert 85.7 % , Mountaineer Zwarn 78.3 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"We are currently gathering silk. A donation of sixty pieces of silk cloth will net you full recognition by our people for your generous actions\nIf you currently have sixty pieces, you may donate them now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":64,"y":23,"n":"Raedon Duskstriker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"1318":{"id":1318,"t":"Unfinished Gordok Business","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 6,600, 1.26 times as much.","obj":"Find the Gauntlet of Gordok Might and return it to Captain Kromcrush in Dire Maul.\nAccording to Kromcrush, the \"old timey story\" says that Tortheldrin - a \"creepy\" elf who called himself a prince - stole it from one of the Gordok kings.\nGauntlet of Gordok Might The Prince's Chest","desc":"Now you da king, so maybe you get prized Gordok artifact back from creepy elf who calls himself Prince! Da king before you failed, just like all da other kings since Tortheldrin - da creepy elf - stole it from old timey Gordok king!\nArtifact is called da Gauntlet of Gordok Might. Old timey stories say only da one true king da Gordok can get it back. Old timey story also say creepy elf is still around here - you find it and it will become mighty gauntlet you wear forever! Yar, I show you!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGordok's Handguards Gordok's Gauntlets Gordok's Gloves Gordok's Handwraps\nExperience: 8,300\nSilverpine Forest Open the zone on the world map Level 60 , requires level 56 Difficulty 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 1318","cats":["dire-maul"]},"99158":{"id":99158,"t":"Dawn in the mountains","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the crate of candles to Father Gavin at Misty Pine Refuge.\nProvided: Crate of Candles","desc":"There's a priest out in the mountains that belongs to an organization called the Argent Dawn. They're a holy group that is dedicated to finding and destroying the unholy and unnatural.\nFather Gavin though, he's mostly the type that seeks to help and heal everyone rather than grab a weapon. He's fixed up an old building to serve as a rest spot for travelers and called it Misty Pine Refuge. I've got a shipment of holy candles that I need to get him. Could you bring them to him if your going that way?","back":"Why did the Light guide you here today?","done":"Ah. Candles from Ironforge.\nWhile I am mostly able to live independently in my hermitage, there are a few key things that I appreciate from the city and the pious.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.2,"y":52.2,"n":"Maxan Anvol","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Father Gavin","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"1238":{"id":1238,"t":"The Lost Report","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Spy's Report to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.\nSpy's Report\nProvided: Spy's Report","desc":"Sifting through the loose dirt, the severed hand of an orc is found. And clutched in the hand is a bone-carved tube. And in the tube is a dirt-stained parchment.\nThe parchment is a report made by an orc who spent weeks spying on the city of Theramore.\nAfter scanning the parchment, it is clear that it must be brought to the orc spymaster in Brackenwall Village.","rew":"Experience: 2,050\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You have something for me?","done":"Good work, ‹name›. Our agent, Marg Nighteye, was stationed outside Theramore. He was charged to spy on the city.\nThis is his latest report, and it may be his last -- from your testimony, I fear that Marg met his end in the swamp...","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":55.4,"y":25.9,"n":"Loose Dirt","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":35.2,"y":30.7,"n":"Nazeer Bloodpike","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"3638":{"id":3638,"t":"The Pledge of Secrecy","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you agree to become a Goblin Engineer, then right-click on the Pledge of Secrecy and speak once more with Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan.\nNixx's Signed Pledge\nProvided: Nixx's Pledge of Secrecy","desc":"Goblin engineering is about practical uses for high profit and higher explosive power! Our schemata allow us to make powerful bombs and mighty weaponry; the manual you read covered this.\nThe manual also covered our ages old oath of secrecy on our schemata. Once you become a goblin engineer, that's that. There is no access to gnome engineering at all.\nIf you still want to become a goblin engineer, sign this document pledging life-long secrecy and speak with me again. Think about it carefully, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"If you've signed the document and are ready to hand it to me, then that is that. You've been told that this is a one way trip. If you're ready, then hop on board!","done":"Welcome aboard, Goblin Engineer ‹name›! You soon will have access to the most powerful engineering schemata anywhere on Azeroth.\nNow that you have committed yourself to the pursuit of this knowledge, it is time to examine your goblin-oriented engineering work. From there, we'll help you build a plan to maximize your goblin engineering talents!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.3,"n":"Nixx Sprocketspring","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"5158":{"id":5158,"t":"Seeking Spiritual Aid","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Corrupt Moon Well Water to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.\nCorrupt Moonwell Water\nProvided: Corrupt Moonwell Water","desc":"Take the corrupt water to the Barrens, ‹name›. South of Ratchet, hidden along the shore, is an old friend of mine, a shaman named Islen Waterseer. She is a powerful shaman who will help us. Her relationship with the spirits of water has always been strong. Our task being a noble one should be enough to persuade her and the spirits of water to aid us in this task.\nYou should find her at a small camp right along the water's edge. And, ‹name›, ignore the pirates... they are but a nuisance and no threat to you.","rew":"Experience: 2,550","back":"I sense you are not just a simple traveler looking for the path to Ratchet. Come, sit and rest at our camp. Speak to me when you're ready.","done":"Ah, you need the water from this Moon Well cleansed. Stopping this force of malice in Felwood seems noble enough, but it is not for me to decide if the water will be purified. I will ask the spirits of water--it will be up to them to decide if the cause is just.\nGive me a moment and I will tell them of your plea. I hope they are as sympathetic as I am to your cause.\nFelwood The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.2,"y":82.1,"n":"Greta Mosshoof","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Islen Waterseer","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4118":{"id":4118,"t":"Corrupted Songflower","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply some Cenarion plant salve to the songflower. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":40.1,"y":56.5,"n":"Corrupted Songflower","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"998":{"id":998,"t":"Corrupted Windblossom","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":55.8,"y":7,"n":"Corrupted Windblossom","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"518":{"id":518,"t":"The Crown of Will","lv":39,"min":34,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Crushridge Maulers for Melisara in Tarren Mill.\nCrushridge Mauler slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Mug'Thol and his Crushridge ogres have overrun the ruins of Alterac. It will be hard to inflict any serious punishment upon him without thinning out the ogres' numbers.\nAfter softening them up, we'll proceed.\nUnderstood? Good. Now go.","rew":"Experience: 2,250\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I note that your task is unfinished, ‹name›. Shall I inform Sharlindra of your ineptitude?","done":"The snow blooms red with the blood of the ogres, but we cannot cease our efforts until the spirit and numbers of the Crushridge have been crushed and ground into the dirt and snow.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.6,"y":20.6,"n":"Melisara","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"9318":{"id":9318,"t":"Blessed Wizard Oil","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0.","obj":"8 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nBlessed Wizard Oil","back":"In exchange for the necrotic runes of the Scourge invaders, the Argent Dawn will give you one vial of blessed wizard oil.","done":"I hope that you will find these items useful in future battles.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.8,"y":30.7,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.9,"y":72.6,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.1,"y":45.4,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"2038":{"id":2038,"t":"Bingles' Missing Supplies","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and return Bingles' supplies:\nBingles' Wrench, Bingles' Screwdriver, Bingles' Hammer, and Bingles' Blastencapper.\nBingles' Wrench Bingles's Toolbucket\nBingles' Screwdriver Bingles's Toolbucket\nBingles' Hammer Bingles's Toolbucket\nBingles' Blastencapper Bingles's Blastencapper","desc":"As if crashing into the Loch wasn't bad enough, troggs from the nearby island attacked me and stole my tools and special Blastenheimer Blastencapper explosives. With no gyrocopter and no explosives, the movement has no chance!\nGet my tools back and find my Blastencapper explosives, ‹name›. For Gnomeregan!","rew":"You will receive:\nBingles' Flying Gloves\nMoney: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"‹name›! Where are my things?!","done":"You've done the movement a great service, ‹name›. The troggs and leper gnomes infesting Gnomeregan will soon feel the brunt of a gnomish air assault!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":63.6,"y":47.9,"n":"Bingles Blastenheimer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"86758":{"id":86758,"t":"Twisting the knife","lv":16,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find and defeat the crocolisk Daggerfang and bring back Marek's knife.\nMarek's Croc-Hunting Knife","desc":"Did I ever tell you how I almost lost me hand to a crocolisk? Managed to jam me knife into its jaw, and scrambled out real quick. I thought I had the knife around here somewhere, but I can't seem to find it.\nAnyway, that croc is probably still out there hunting along the edge of the lake. That nasty brute probably needs to go, for the safety of the other hunters, if nothing else.\nI've taken to calling it Daggerfang. If you see it, give it a friendly hello from me! And by \"hello\" I mean \"stab.\"","rew":"You will receive:\nDaggerfang's Daggerfang\nMoney: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"How goes the huntin'?","done":"Hah! You did it! I never thought that ol' croc would get its comeuppance, but that does the trick!\nOh ah... y'know, I had to get me another knife, but maybe that one will bring you some good luck. Why don't you hang onto it?","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":81.8,"y":61.8,"n":"Marek Ironheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"278":{"id":278,"t":"A Dark Threat Looms","lv":18,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Chief Engineer Hinderweir wants you to gather Lurker Venom, a Mo'grosh Crystal, and a Crocolisk Tear.\nLurker Venom Cliff Lurker 10 % , Wood Lurker 10 % , Forest Lurker 10 % , Shanda the Spinner 10 %\nMo'grosh Crystal Emogg the Crusher 5 % , Mo'grosh Mystic 5 % , Mo'grosh Shaman 5 % , Mo'grosh Brute 5 % and 2 more\nCrocolisk Tear Loch Crocolisk 10 % , Large Loch Crocolisk 10 %","desc":"Begin collecting the disarming materials immediately, ‹name›. Lurker Venom can be found on the indigenous spiders in Loch Modan. Crocolisk tears are found here in the Loch as well. But a Mo'Grosh crystal will be very difficult to procure. The ogres to the northeast mine them but the crystals are a very rare commodity.\nWe need to be prepared to defuse a Dark Iron attack! Return to me once you've collected the needed items and I will prepare the mixture.","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Do you have the needed items? Time is of the essence!!","done":"Just in time, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":46,"y":13.6,"n":"Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8678":{"id":8678,"t":"Proudhorn the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":73,"y":23.4,"n":"Elder Proudhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1958":{"id":1958,"t":"Celestial Power","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCelestial Orb Celestial Stave\nExperience: 3,150","done":"You should be proud of yourself, ‹name›. Many mages have fallen to the creatures you faced.\nThe Celestial Orb is ready. Or if you'd like I can mount it atop a staff. It's up to you. I'd prefer the orb, but who am I to judge?","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"758":{"id":758,"t":"Thunderhorn Cleansing","lv":8,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Thunderhorn Cleansing Totem at the Thunderhorn Water Well, then return to Mull.\nProvided: Thunderhorn Cleansing Totem","desc":"The totem is ready, ‹name›. And again, it is your task to perform the ritual of cleansing.\nGo to the Thunderhorn Water Well, north of the village, and use the Thunderhorn Cleansing Totem in your ritual. After you do this, return to me.\nMay the spirits guide you.","rew":"You will receive:\nThunderhorn Cloak\nExperience: 700\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The Thunderhorn Water Well is still tainted, ‹name›. Please, you must perform the ritual!","done":"Ancestors of the Thunderhorn clan spoke to me in a dream, praising you for your actions near their well.\nFor their gratitude, they wish to give you this...","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.5,"y":63.6,"n":"Mull Thunderhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9078":{"id":9078,"t":"Bonescythe Legplates","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -100g instead of 0.","obj":"Rohan the Assassin at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Bonescythe Legplates if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Legplates, 20 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar, 8 Cured Rugged Hides and 100 gold pieces.\nDesecrated Legplates\n20 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n8 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"If you want Bonescythe made, you're going to have to supply the materials.\nEnter Naxxramas, the big floating city of death in the sky up there, and find desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps. Bring those back along with the materials to put everything together and you'll have your Bonescythe. Oh, and you'll need to pay me for my troubles... I'll supply the bones.","rew":"You will receive:\nBonescythe Legplates\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"<Rohan laughs.>\nI just realized the irony in all of this.","done":"Be careful walking around in those things. You might cut yourself.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.9,"n":"Rohan the Assassin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9238":{"id":9238,"t":"Glacial Wrists","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -200g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 4 Frozen Runes, 2 Bolts of Runecloth, 2 Essences of Water, 2 Ironweb Spider Silks and 200 gold.\n4 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n2 Bolt of Runecloth Felsteel Chest 0.9 % , Twilight Lord Everun 0 %\n2 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\n2 Ironweb Spider Silk Mother Smolderweb 50 % , Crystal Fang 47 % , Gretheer 16.2 % , Plague Lurker 13.9 % and 4 more","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion, may he rest in peace, I am now able to create Glacial wrists. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nGlacial Wrists","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8918":{"id":8918,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Bindings of Elements to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\n15 Silithus Venom Sample Stonelash Scorpid 30 % , Stonelash Pincer 30 % , Stonelash Flayer 30 % , Sand Skitterer 30 % and 1 more\nBindings of Elements Crypt Beast 4.8 % in Stratholme , Crypt Crawler 4.1 % in Stratholme , Crimson Monk 3 % in Stratholme , Splintered Skeleton 1.5 % in Scholomance","desc":"Hail, ‹class›! I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world. Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.\nPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.\nI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus. Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","rew":"You will receive:\nBindings of The Five Thunders\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you obtained the items I require, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, yes. That old goblin shall be quite happy with this blood.\nThose bindings were part of a larger armor set. If you're interested in providing me with further assistance I'd be willing to consider parting with the rest of it.\nOrgrimmar Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8998":{"id":8998,"t":"Back to the Beginning","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mokvar at Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom.","desc":"I suppose that this is goodbye then, my friend. But, I'll always be here if you want to come back and talk with me from time to time. Probably while you're loitering around waiting for your buddies to join you for a raid on Blackrock Spire.\nGo, before I start to cry. Go back to Mokvar in Orgrimmar and tell him what's happened.","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"I am pleased to see that you have survived, ‹name›. You look well, if not a bit more seasoned.\nCome, tell me of all that has transpired.\nBurning Steppes Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"94438":{"id":94438,"t":"A lesson in divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Take the Symbol of Life and use it to resurrect Deathguard Falgan at Venomweb Vale.\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement.\nTake the Symbol of Life and use it to resurrect Deathguard Falgan at Venomweb Vale.","desc":"Falgan and I were sent on a mission to scout out scarlet activity in Venomweb Vale. We managed to sneak close enough to one of their camps to hear about new orders involving an attack on Brill. Before we could decide what to do next, I stepped on a twig and the noise alerted them to us.\nFalgan yelled at me to run, so I ran. By the time I realized he wasn't with me, I was halfway to Brill. That brave idiot probably stayed behind to hold them off for me.\nPlease, find my friend and help him if you can.","done":"I'm... back? And saved by a ‹class› no less? I see you carry a Symbol of Life. I've not seen one of those since... well, since before the war when Lordaeron was a very different place. I can only assume you are here to help. Billmuth and I were sent here to scout out the scarlet activity here, and we found out that they are planning some kind of attack.\nIf you would be willing to help more, there may yet be more than you can do to help the Forsaken.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Deathguard Billmuth","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":86.6,"y":47.6,"n":"Deathguard Falgan","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"2998":{"id":2998,"t":"Tome of Divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.","desc":"Greetings, brother/sister. Duthorian Rall, one of our most influential paladins, was speaking about you recently. I overheard him talking about how it was time you be put to the test some... along with some very complimentary things about how well you've performed thus far.\nIf I were you, I'd head to Stormwind and speak to him when you have time. I'm sure he's in the Cathedral of Light--that's where he spends most of his time.","rew":"Experience: 230","done":"It is beautiful here in Stormwind, is it not?\nYour timing actually couldn't have been better, ‹name›.\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.1,"y":66,"n":"Brother Wilhelm","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7638":{"id":7638,"t":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind's Cathedral District.","desc":"The time has come, ‹name›, for you to learn about what it will take for you to acquire something you have no doubt waited on for some time... your charger.\nSpeak with Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker here in Stormwind's Cathedral District. It is he who will guide you not only though the legerdemain of a Paladin's most trusted mount, but the tasks before you to acquire one of your own.\nI wish you the best in this trial. For the Light, noble brother/sister!","rew":"Experience: 650\n+10 reputation with Stormwind","done":"I am glad to see you ‹name›. I know that you have awaited word as to how to acquire your charger, and now that time has come.\nYou will be surely tested in many different ways, but most importantly in your willingness to rise above numerous obstacles thrust before you. These are not done as a learning exercise - your stature is beyond simple educational tests. You must save your future companion from the clutches of the evil you have spent your life fighting.\nTake heed, your time has come!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5638":{"id":5638,"t":"Desperate Prayer","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","desc":"Just a short time ago, one of your priests was here looking for you, ‹race›. He said that if I were to see you, I should direct you towards the Cathedral of Light. He said it was very important, but I would not be overly concerned if I were you. His demeanor seemed positive... as though it were good news. I wouldn't take too long in making my way there if I were you.\nElune be with you, good ‹race›.","rew":"You will learn: Desperate Prayer\nExperience: 210","done":"I'm glad you've arrived, ‹name›. There are many things we will have to discuss, but most importantly is your training in the ways of the Light.\nThere are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we'll begin discussing some of those now.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":35.7,"y":63.2,"n":"Nara Meideros","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":44.6,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"118":{"id":118,"t":"The Price of Shoes","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Verner's Note to Smith Argus in Goldshire.\nVerner's Note\nProvided: Verner's Note","desc":"I've been using so much iron keeping the Stormwind Guards outfitted, I don't have enough to supply the stable's horses with shoes!\nTake this note to Blacksmith Argus in Goldshire. It explains to him my problem and requests a shipment of horseshoes.","rew":"Experience: 340\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What's that? Verner sent you, you say? Well give me his note. And SPEAK UP!","done":"Heh, so old Verner needs some shoes, does he!?!\nRedridge Mountains Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":25.9,"y":47.3,"n":"Verner Osgood","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.7,"y":65.5,"n":"Smith Argus","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8838":{"id":8838,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with the Gnomeregan exiles.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":28.5,"n":"Officer Porterhouse","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"2358":{"id":2358,"t":"Horns of Nez'ra","lv":22,"min":16,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Horns of Nez'ra to Arantir's Shadow in Lakeshire.\nHorns of Nez'ra Blackrock Gladiator , Blackrock Summoner , Blackrock Hunter , Blackrock Sentry and 4 more","desc":"Many years ago, the Horns of Nez'ra were stolen from Ravenholdt manor. Across continents and oceans I have searched, only to discover that these insignificant beasts have had it in their possession all along.\nSlay every Blackrock orc you cross until the Horns of Nez'ra are recovered. Should you recover the horns, find me in Lakeshire.\nDo this for me and your name shall be known to Ravenholdt, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Thistle Tea\nExperience: 1,800","back":"Do you have the demon prince's horns?","done":"To deny Ravenholdt the artifact, would be to deny one's own existence. Well done, ‹class›. You may yet walk among the assassins of Ravenholdt.\nAs a young rogue adventuring in Darkshore, I discovered a tea that replenishes energy in combat. It has served me well throughout the years and now I pass on a taste of the thistle tea to you. Drink of it when you tire, ‹name›, and fight with vigor once more!","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":23,"y":52.3,"n":"Arantir","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"8358":{"id":8358,"t":"Incoming Gumdrop","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Do a train emote at Kali Remik, and in exchange you'll receive a Darkspear Gumdrop!","desc":"A trick-or-treater! Yeah mon!\nWell now, even though you're doing something noble and collecting candies for a sick child, I can't let you off the hook that easily. I have a yummy Darkspear Gumdrop to give to the sick child... if you make a train noise for me! Haha, yes, that'll be the trick! The price of this gumdrop is one train noise!\nChugga-chugga, ‹class›!","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkspear Gumdrop","back":"Well, go ahead now...","done":"Woo-woo! Well done, ‹name›! Here's your treat.\nHappy Hallow's End!","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":56.1,"y":74.2,"n":"Kali Remik","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8278":{"id":8278,"t":"Noggle's Last Hope","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Beetix Ficklespragg at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to gather 3 Stonelash Pincer Stingers, 3 Stonelash Flayer Stingers and 3 Rock Stalker Fangs.\n3 Stonelash Flayer Stinger Stonelash Flayer 80 %\n3 Stonelash Pincer Stinger Stonelash Pincer 80 %\n3 Rock Stalker Fang Rock Stalker 80 %","desc":"Blasted! The antidote didn't work. Noggle must've been stung by one of the stronger creatures in the far south.\nI'm going to need you to go there and get me some more samples, ‹name›. The good news is that since their poison is stronger I won't require as many. The bad news is that there are more kinds of poisonous creatures crawling around the southern area so you'll have to draw from more sources.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n2 Major Healing Potion Major Mana Potion\nMoney: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,000\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"This is our last chance to save Noggle! Hurry!","done":"Yes! It seems to be working, Noggle is coming to. We owe ya big time!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.6,"y":38.6,"n":"Beetix Ficklespragg","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"438":{"id":438,"t":"The Decrepit Ferry","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the Decrepit Ferry.\nSearch for the reason the Scourge are there.","desc":"‹name›, we've discovered a new hive for the Scourge: the Decrepit Ferry. The ferry lies east of the Sepulcher, and is heavily patrolled by rot hides and other undead.\nThere must be a reason for the Scourge's occupation of the area. Go to the Decrepit Ferry and find out why the Scourge are there.","rew":"Experience: 875\n+75 reputation with Undercity","done":"Heaped within this boat is a pile of wrapped corpses. And looking east across Lordamere Lake, an opposing dock on Fenris Isle can be seen.\nThe fate of the corpses must lie on Fenris Isle.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":40.9,"n":"High Executor Hadrec","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":58.4,"y":34.9,"n":"Corpse Laden Boat","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1558":{"id":1558,"t":"The Stonewrought Dam","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the orphan to the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan. You should take him to the middle of the dam so he can see out over the giant waterfall.","desc":"Ironforge is where all the dwarves and gnomes live. Near there is a place called Loch Modan, and the dwarves built a HUGE dam there. They say it's one of the biggest things anyone's ever made. Wow!\nCould you take me to Loch Modan and see the dam there, please? I think it is the Stone... um... Stonewrench Dam? Stonewrought? It's big - that's for sure. I'd like to look out over the big waterfall. I promise I won't lean over too far!","rew":"Experience: 650\n+50 reputation with Alliance","back":"Are we there yet?","done":"WOW - the dam was WAY bigger than I thought! I could barely hear myself talk from the sound of all the rushing water! Hey, do you think it would ever run out of water? Man, what would happen if that damn ever broke! WOW, that would be scary!\nThanks for taking me to see the dam. That was very kind of you. I told you I wouldn't lean over too far!\nLoch Modan Open the zone on the world map Start Human Orphan End Human Orphan Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Alliance Shareable No Quest ID 1558\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 650 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Children's Week\nUse the Human Orphan Whistle to talk with the child you will be looking after during Children's Week.\nOrphan Matron Nightingale Stormwind City\n2 [ 60 ] The Stonewrought Dam this quest\nTake the orphan to the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan.\nHuman Orphan\n650 XP","cats":["special"]},"1078":{"id":1078,"t":"Retrieval for Mauren","lv":26,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Crystalized Scales to Collin Mauren in Stormwind.\n8 Crystalized Scales Scorched Basilisk 20 % , Blackened Basilisk 20 % , Saltstone Basilisk 20 % , Singed Basilisk 20 %","desc":"Travelers keep asking me about the Stonetalon Mountains. It seems to be a popular place for adventure--it doesn't matter if you're seeking wyvern, elementals, or you have business with the Venture Co.\nWithin the Charred Vale, deep in Stonetalon, there used to be a species of basilisks whose scales, when ground to dust, made a wonderful reagent for some spells I've created.\nIf those basilisks still live, I would love to have a few of their scales.\nTake your time, it is no rush, but I can pay well.","rew":"You will receive:\nSpellcrafter Wand\nExperience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hello again, ‹name›.\nHave you already returned from the Vale in Stonetalon with those scales?","done":"This is perfect, ‹name›. Thank you greatly.\nPerhaps one day in the future I'll be able to help you as you have helped me.\nStormwind City Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":53,"y":86.6,"n":"Collin Mauren","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"198":{"id":198,"t":"Supplies to Private Thorsen","lv":32,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Miscellaneous Goblin Supplies to Private Thorsen.\nMiscellaneous Goblin Supplies\nProvided: Miscellaneous Goblin Supplies","desc":"Hmm. Yes, I do have something you could do, actually. Lieutenant Doren and his followers up in the north need their regular supplies from us.\nThey haven't been delivered, and with the trolls attacking, I'll need someone to do it. Doren's camp lies northwest of the road at the entrance to Stranglethorn from Duskwood. Give the supplies to Private Thorsen, if he's not in the camp, then he'll be patrolling south of it. He'll take care of them.\nMind you, if you fail, you'll owe me restitution.","rew":"Money: 16 0 gold, 16 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes? What do you want? Oh, supplies from the goblins. Strange seeing a ‹race› delivering them, usually they send their own. No matter... you didn't touch them did you? Good good... we wouldn't want anything to happen to our mines, oh no.","done":"These land mines will help us defend ourselves from that animal Kurzen and his men. Thank you for bringing them. If you need further work, I can probably find something for you to do. And you won't have to deal with those goblins, hm?","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":77.2,"n":"Krazek","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3.4,"n":"Private Thorsen","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"598":{"id":598,"t":"Split Bone Necklace","lv":42,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 25 Split Bone Necklaces to Kin'weelay at the Grom'gol Base camp.\n25 Split Bone Necklace Ana'thek the Cruel 10 % , Skullsplitter Beastmaster 10 % , Skullsplitter Berserker 10 % , Skullsplitter Scout 10 % and 4 more","desc":"Now that you have gathered Bloodscalp trophies, I have another task for you. The Skullsplitter tribe of trolls live to the southeast, and for years we have warred with them. Although the Darkspears no longer dwell in Stranglethorn, we are bound to our conflict with the Skullsplitters.\nSo, hunt them. Gather their Split Bone Necklaces and return to me. Aid us in our war, and you will earn the friendship of the Darkspears.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDarkspear Shoes Darkspear Boots\nExperience: 3,450\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"The Skullsplitters will curse the day they brought us to war! Is your task complete?","done":"Your strength is great to have gained these necklaces, ‹name›. The Skullsplitters fall to you like young saplings stomped to earth by a Basilisk!\nYour deeds are a boon to us.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.3,"y":27.7,"n":"Kin'weelay","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1398":{"id":1398,"t":"Driftwood","lv":42,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 pieces of Sundried Driftwood to Watcher Biggs in the Swamp of Sorrows.\n8 Sundried Driftwood Sundried Driftwood","desc":"I owe you greatly, ‹name›. An honorable heart beats within you. And now I have another task for which I humbly ask your aid.\nIf I'm ever to reach Nethergarde, then I must fix this wagon. And for that... I will need wood. Strong, dry wood--not the spongy, tangled wood of the swamp's trees.\n‹name›, go east to the coast and search for driftwood that has been dried by the sun. Bring it to me.","rew":"Experience: 3,450\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you find any driftwood, ‹name›?","done":"This wood is light, but tough. Thank you, ‹name›. It will work nicely.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":26.7,"y":59.8,"n":"Watcher Biggs","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"1878":{"id":1878,"t":"Water Pouch Bounty","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Wastewander Water Pouch Andre Firebeard 35 % , Wastewander Scofflaw 35 % , Wastewander Assassin 35 % , Wastewander Bandit 35 % and 3 more","rew":"You will receive:\nGadgetzan Water Co. Care Package\nExperience: 380\n+10 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Back again, ‹name›? If you have five more Wastewander water pouches, then I have a care package with your name on it!","done":"Excellent - the more water pouches we are able to reclaim, the further away from disaster we'll all be! Keep 'em coming, and I will be sure to reward you for every five water pouches you bring me.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":28.4,"n":"Spigot Operator Luglunket","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8598":{"id":8598,"t":"rAnS0m","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Ransom Letter to Narain Soothfancy in Tanaris.\nRansom Letter\nProvided: Ransom Letter","desc":"<The text on this note is made up of various typefaces glued onto the parchment's surface.>\nWe've got your precious book, gnome. If you ever want to see it again, you'll do exactly as we ask.\n<A detailed set of instructions is listed, spanning 3 pages.>\nBring the money and come alone!","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+10 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Say, what's the matter?","done":"<Narain's face glows a bright red.>\nBooknap my... book, will they!? I'll teach them what it means to mess with a psychic gnome!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.8,"y":129.7,"n":"Freshly Dug Dirt","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8758":{"id":8758,"t":"The Path of the Invoker","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Your continued defense of the children of Kalimdor has been acknowledged. Hand me your signet ring so that I may enhance its powers.","done":"Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, ‹name›. May you never stray from the path of the invoker!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2438":{"id":2438,"t":"The Emerald Dreamcatcher","lv":6,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Emerald Dreamcatcher to Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.\nEmerald Dreamcatcher Tallonkai's Dresser","desc":"I was once given an emerald dreamcatcher from Gaerolas Talvethen, the warden of the druids in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. This powerful amulet is able to siphon energy from the Emerald Dream, bestowing luck upon those who carry it.\nSadly, I have not been able to retrieve it from my dresser in Starbreeze Village... Although Starbreeze was once a tranquil place, it has now succumbed to the corruption of the furbolg that reside there.\nPerhaps you would be willing to recover my dreamcatcher, ‹class›?","rew":"Money: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 410\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Please move swiftly. I can only hope that my emerald dreamcatcher has been unharmed by the furbolg.\nHave you recovered it yet, ‹name›?","done":"My emerald dreamcatcher is of great importance to me. It is a gift only given to few. Thank you for returning it, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.6,"y":56.9,"n":"Tallonkai Swiftroot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"918":{"id":918,"t":"Timberling Seeds","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Timberling Seeds to Denelan at Lake Al'Ameth.\n8 Timberling Seed Elder Timberling , Timberling 37 % , Oakenscowl 20 % , Timberling Mire Beast 20 % and 2 more","desc":"The timberlings of Teldrassil are elementals of nature. In some ways they reflect the natural order of plants and animals on our great tree.\nSo it is disturbing to see how angry the timberlings have become.\nI believe it has something to do with the soil. I have been working on different methods of nurturing plants and would like to try them on timberling seeds. Please, can you gather seeds from timberlings around Lake Al'Ameth and bring them to me?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Forest Mushroom Cap\nExperience: 625\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Do you have the seeds? I am eager to plant them.","done":"You got them. This is good!\nI will plant these seeds in special soil I have prepared. I believe the seeds will sprout into timberlings who are much more docile. Perhaps later you can see the results!","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Denalan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"358":{"id":358,"t":"Graverobbers","lv":8,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Rot Hide Graverobbers and Rot Hide Mongrels.\nBring 8 Embalming Ichors to Magistrate Sevren in Brill.\n8 Embalming Ichor Rot Hide Graverobber 40 % , Rot Hide Mongrel 40 % , Rot Hide Gnoll 40 %\nRot Hide Graverobber slain : 0/ 8\nRot Hide Mongrel slain : 0/ 5","desc":"The Mass Graves, southwest of Garren's Haunt to the north, were made to accommodate the...impressive...number of deaths Tirisfal suffered when the Plague first came.\nThe bodies in these graves have so far been spared an undeath, but the Scourge now send Rot Hide Gnolls to gather the corpses and use them to bolster their armies. This cannot be allowed!\nYour task is twofold: slay the Rot Hides at the Mass Grave and Garren's Haunt, and gather from them the Embalming Ichor that gives them life.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCold Steel Gauntlets Zombie Skin Boots\nMoney: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Is your task complete? Have you destroyed those dog-things and drained them of their ichor?","done":"Expertly done, ‹name›. The Scourge are mistaken if they think they can use those corpses against us, and the fluid you gathered from the Rot Hide slaves will be studied by our Apothecaries. It may have secrets we can use against them.\nAs I said, well done. But our struggle continues, and the conflict will surely offer you more chances to prove your worth to the Forsaken.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.3,"y":50.8,"n":"Magistrate Sevren","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"97558":{"id":97558,"t":"Hides for the forsaken","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Shelene Rhobart 8 Duskbat Wing Membranes, 6 Darkhound Hides and 3 Vile Fin Murloc Skin.\n8 Duskbat Wing Membrane\n6 Darkhound Hide\n3 Vile Fin Murloc Skin","desc":"One part of undeath no one mentions is what happens when we are injured. How does the skin of an undead heal itself?\nWell, it doesn't.\nOurs is a cursed life, ‹name›. We must take from the living to further our own existence.\nWhen we sustain an injury, we must replace our skin which usually means animal hides. Since different hide thicknesses are better for different places on our bodies a variety is key!\nBring me wing membranes of a duskbat, hides from a darkhound and skin of a Vile Fin murloc.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPatchwing Pants Howlhide Vest Finscale Soles\nMoney: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you gathered the skin I inquired about? Our stocks are running low.\nIt may seem odd to ask for murloc skin but it works well for internal membranes, or surfaces like cheeks or mouths.\nSimilarly, the duskbat wing membranes are especially suited for more delicate areas, like faces or fingers. It prevents the skin from being too... thick.","done":"Ah, excellent! Thank you for acquiring these. I can promise they will be put to good use.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.4,"y":60,"n":"Shelene Rhobart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2198":{"id":2198,"t":"The Shattered Necklace","lv":41,"min":37,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search for the original creator of the shattered necklace to learn of its potential value.\nShattered Necklace Stonevault Cave Hunter 8 % , Stonevault Oracle 8 % , Stonevault Rockchewer 8 % , Shadowforge Digger 8 % and 2 more\nProvided: Shattered Necklace","desc":"You have found a tarnished necklace, though the tarnish belies intricate and magical craftsmanship. The necklace has been shattered, as its setting appears to be missing three gems. On the underside of the necklace is the faint imprint of the city seal for Ironforge. Below the seal are three tiny, engraved letters: \"TdK\".\nIf there is anything to be gleaned from the necklace, you will need to learn about its origins. Perhaps the seal and the initials are a start...","rew":"Experience: 3,300","back":"You've got the wrong gnome, pal! I was never there! You can't prove anything!\nWait a second... who are you? What the... where did you find this necklace at?","done":"Yes... I am the jeweler who made this necklace. I also am not in the business of handing out information as though it were free. Information is never free, friend. If I am going to help you out, you need to help ME out first.\nDun Morogh Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.9,"y":21.7,"n":"Talvash del Kissel","e":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"2278":{"id":2278,"t":"The Platinum Discs","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with stone watcher and learn what ancient lore it keeps. Once you have learned what lore it has to offer, activate the Discs of Norgannon.","desc":"The centerpieces of this treasure chamber are four huge platinum discs, each adorned with numerous sigils of an unknown origin. Touching them makes your hand tingle. Just after touching the discs, the visage of a large stone watcher springs forth.\n\"Salutations. I am a keeper of knowledge. The Creators' synthesis of the Earthen has been chronicled and stored here for this world in the Discs of Norgannon.\"\nYou have uncovered a wealth of previously undiscovered worldly lore!","rew":"Experience: 4,200","back":"The voice of the stone watcher seems to resonate within your very inner being:\n\"You must first satisfy the data assimilation prerequisite of Discs of Norgannon; once you fulfill this requirement, you will then be permitted to obtain a portable version of the stored data. Please be sure you have fully explored the information within this repository first.\"","done":"Following the instructions of the stone watcher, you once again access the Discs of Norgannon now that you have learned about the history of the Earthen, the troggs, and the dwarves. A faint, brief hum is heard from within the discs. The stone watcher then speaks:\n\"The discs have now been synthesized. Access the Discs of Norgannon once more to receive your personal copy.\"\nStart The Discs of Norgannon End The Discs of Norgannon Level 47 , requires level 40 Difficulty 40 43 45 50 59 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 2278\nThe chain\n14 quests from level 47 to 50, 40,920 XP in all.\n1 [ 47 ] The Platinum Discs this quest\nSpeak with stone watcher and learn what ancient lore it keeps.\nThe Discs of Norgannon\n4,200 XP\n2 [ 47 ] The Platinum Discs\nTake the miniature version of the Discs of Norgannon to the Explorers' League in Ironforge.\nThe Discs of Norgannon\n5,250 XP\n[ 47 ] The Platinum Discs\nTake the miniature version of the Discs of Norgannon to the one of the sages in Thunder Bluff.\nThe Discs of Norgannon\n5,250 XP\n3 [ 47 ] The Platinum Discs\nTake your reward voucher to Dinita Stonemantle in the Vault of Ironforge.\nAfter: The Platinum Discs\nHigh Explorer Magellas Dun Morogh\n420 XP\n[ 47 ] The Platinum Discs\nTake the reward voucher to Bena Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff.\nAfter: The Platinum Discs\nSage Truthseeker Thunder Bluff\n420 XP\n4 [ 50 ] Portents of Uldum\nSpeak with Historian Karnik in the Hall of Explorers within Ironforge.\nAfter: The Platinum Discs\nHigh Explorer Magellas Dun Morogh\n470 XP\n[ 50 ] Portents of Uldum\nSpeak with Nara Wildmane on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.\nAfter: The Platinum Discs\nSage Truthseeker Thunder Bluff\n470 XP\n5 [ 50 ] Seeing What Happens\nBring the miniature platinum discs to the gates of Uldum in Tanaris and look for clues as to the connection between the two.\nAfter: Portents of Uldum\nHistorian Karnik Dun Morogh\n4,700 XP\n[ 50 ] Seeing What Happens\nBring the miniature platinum discs to the gates of Uldum in Tanaris and look for clues as to the connection between the two.\nAfter: Portents of Uldum\nNara Wildmane Thunder Bluff\n4,700 XP\n6 [ 50 ] The Stone Watcher\nLearn the purpose of","cats":["uldaman"]},"1478":{"id":1478,"t":"Halgar's Summons","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Carendin Halgar in the Undercity.","desc":"Ah, ‹name›! I just received word from Carendin Halgar that he would like to see you for further training.\nYou should be proud of yourself, ‹name›. It's not every day that Master Halgar personally sees fit to instruct a young warlock.\nYou'll be able to find him in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, near the Temple of the Damned.","rew":"Experience: 210","done":"Good, I see Ageron managed to find you, ‹name›. Let us waste little time with small talk and pleasantries and focus on your training. There is still much you have to learn.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.6,"y":52.7,"n":"Ageron Kargal","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":26,"n":"Carendin Halgar","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1798":{"id":1798,"t":"Seeking Strahad","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Strahad Farsan in the Barrens.","desc":"It is time you learned the felhunter summoning, ‹name›. I do not have the reagents and items necessary to teach you here, so you will have to seek out another, Strahad Farsan, another of our inner circle.\nHe makes his residence in the goblin port of Ratchet. I will send word ahead of you to inform him of your coming.","rew":"Experience: 600","done":"‹name›? Ah, of course. Our latest prodigy. The real thing can not live up to the legend, I am afraid.\nNo matter, you have come here to learn, not to hear me make jokes to myself.\nStormwind City The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85.2,"n":"Gakin the Darkbinder","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1638":{"id":1638,"t":"A Warrior's Training","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Harry Burlguard.","desc":"You've shown yourself to be a competent warrior, ‹name›. But you're still young and have a lot to learn.\nSpeak with Harry Burlguard--he's usually in the Pig and Whistle tavern, in the Old Town of Stormwind. Harry is an old veteran and a good teacher. He can show you a few moves that'll keep you breathing longer.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Oh ho! Have a drink with me, ‹name›. You look tough on the outside, but let's see if your gut can handle a few mugs of the Pig and Whistle's strongest!!\nOr... were you here for a lesson?\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.1,"y":65.8,"n":"Lyria Du Lac","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.4,"y":59.8,"n":"Ilsa Corbin","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.1,"y":53.3,"n":"Harry Burlguard","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1718":{"id":1718,"t":"The Islander","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Klannoc Macleod.","desc":"Your renown as a warrior grows, ‹name›. Now it is time to pit yourself against your peers and see where you stand.\nThere is an island off the coast of the Barrens, south of Ratchet. It is called Fray Island and it is a place where warriors meet.\nMeet, and fight.\nSpeak with the chief warrior of Fray Island, Klannoc Macleod. If he finds you worthy, then Klannoc will lead you further down the warrior's path.\nTo reach Fray Island, search for the sand bar shallows along the Merchant Coast.","rew":"Experience: 600","done":"Hello, ‹name›. It's good to see you made it to Fray Island. I hope you find it to your liking...\nThunder Bluff Orgrimmar Undercity Dun Morogh Stormwind City Darnassus The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":57.2,"y":87.4,"n":"Torm Ragetotem","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":80.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Sorek","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":47.4,"y":17.3,"n":"Baltus Fowler","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.4,"y":35.6,"n":"Kelv Sternhammer","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.6,"y":59.9,"n":"Wu Shen","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58.9,"y":35.3,"n":"Darnath Bladesinger","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":68.6,"y":49.2,"n":"Klannoc Macleod","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"838":{"id":838,"t":"Scholomance","lv":55,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Apothecary Dithers at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.","desc":"On the island of Caer Darrow lies Scholomance - a school that serves as a stronghold for the Scourge. Our enemy dwells within, safely allowed to pursue research that strengthens their power. A door bars the way, and try as we might no entry is to be had without a proper key.\nApothecary Dithers is well versed on Scholomance, and has an idea how to obtain a key. You have proved your value to me as someone who can get things done; I now entrust this task to you. Speak with him on this matter.","rew":"Experience: 550","done":"Yes, ‹class›, the High Executor mentioned you might be the one to trust in the matter of the key. I've dedicated a fair portion of my recent studies to the Scholomance, and I believe I know a means by which you can acquire one that will let you past the front door at will.\nThis task will not be easy, but such tasks seldom are. You most assuredly look like the type to know this as fact.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":68.9,"n":"High Executor Derrington","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.3,"y":69.2,"n":"Apothecary Dithers","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5238":{"id":5238,"t":"Mission Accomplished!","lv":58,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nValiant Shortsword Intrepid Shortsword\nYou will also receive:\nHeroic Commendation Medal\nExperience: 9,300\n+200 reputation with Horde\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","done":"‹name›, your successful re-engineering of the cauldrons is a tremendous victory for us!\n<The commander clears his throat and begins to bellow loudly.>\nLet all within my presence hear: for service to the Kingdom of Stormwind and to the Alliance above and beyond the call of duty - in the face of overwhelming odds and incredible danger, might I add - I give ‹name› this, and I extend upon his/her our undying gratitude as a true hero of the Alliance. Cheers, I say!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":68.9,"n":"High Executor Derrington","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"38":{"id":38,"t":"Westfall Stew","lv":13,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Salma Saldean wants 3 Stringy Vulture Meat, 3 Goretusk Snouts, 3 Murloc Eyes, 3 Okra.\n3 Stringy Vulture Meat Salt Flats Vulture 50.7 % , Salt Flats Scavenger 49.3 % , Greater Fleshripper 37.1 % , Fleshripper 35.2 % and 3 more\n3 Murloc Eye Bluegill Raider 47.2 % , Bluegill Warrior 43.7 % , Blindlight Oracle 43.4 % , Blindlight Muckdweller 42.4 % and 4 more\n3 Goretusk Snout Goretusk 39.2 % , Young Goretusk 37 %\n3 Okra Harvest Reaper 36.5 % , Harvest Watcher 33.2 % , Harvest Golem 30.3 % , Foe Reaper 4000 28 % and 1 more","desc":"Help me make some Westfall Stew! Come back with the following ingredients:\n3 Stringy Vulture Meat\n3 Goretusk Snouts\n3 Murloc Eyes\n3 Okra","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Westfall Stew Recipe: Westfall Stew Salma's Oven Mitts Sharp Kitchen Knife\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Come back with the following ingredients:\n3 Stringy Vulture Meat\n3 Goretusk Snouts\n3 Murloc Eyes\n3 Okra","done":"That Okra will thicken up this broth nicely! Now we just add the Stringy Vulture Meat, a few Murloc Eyes and those delicious Goretusk Snouts. And we're done! For all your help, ‹name›, I want you to take today's first batch of Westfall Stew!","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.4,"y":30.5,"n":"Salma Saldean","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"87318":{"id":87318,"t":"Hearts of the lost","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Search for Corma's partner Essene.","desc":"Thandol Span has been a dangerous place since the Dark Irons blew up the bridge, but I didn't expect to run into them there!\nI managed to escape, but I lost sight of my partner, Essene. I've been searching all over for her, but I haven't found any sign of her. Did the Dark Irons capture her? Did she fall into the river below? Did she make it back to the other side? I don't know! I don't even know if she's alive!\nPlease, if you see any sign of her, let me know!","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":50,"y":12.8,"n":"Corma Villard","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":51.4,"y":9,"n":"Essene Villard","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"88758":{"id":88758,"t":"Sentiments of the lost","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Essene's note back to Corma Villard.\nProvided: Essene's Note","desc":"I just need to finish repacking, and I can get out of here!\nIf you'll do me one last favor, here--take this note to Corma. It'll let her know that I'm alive and I'm on my way!","rew":"You will receive:\nEssene's Hope\nExperience: 2,650","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":51.4,"y":9,"n":"Essene Villard","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":50,"y":12.8,"n":"Corma Villard","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92598":{"id":92598,"t":"The gift of skysight","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use your Skysight racial ability at the Elemental Convergence in Thendal Grove.\nUse Skysight near the Elemental Convergence","desc":"As a Windshaper, you have the ability to use the sacred skysight gifted to us by the elemental spirits. Travel to the standing stones to the northeast of the village. Find the elemental convergence there and use your gift.\nYou'll find that you may draw upon the skysight anywhere, but its boon is much more powerful if you do so in the presence of an elemental convergence. You may at times receive other bits of wisdom from the spirits that are drawn to such places of power, as well.","done":"Like a muscle, your skysight must be exercised if you hope to grow stronger in the gift. Leveraging your skysight to bridge the distance between the mortal and the spiritual may prove invaluable to you in your adventures.\nYou'd do well to remember what you've learned here today. Our ability to use our gifts to hear what the elements tell us could be the key to our survival.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.6,"y":24.4,"n":"Ventaari Brightwish","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93318":{"id":93318,"t":"Wanted vulgara the insatiable","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill Vulgara the Insatiable in the Shen'dar Highlands and bring her head to Danarii Bellowveil.\nVulgara's Head","desc":"By order of Constable Aonda of the Peacekeepers, a bounty is hereby placed upon the scourge of the highlands, Vulgara the Insatiable. Last spotted on a hilltop rise just southwest of Shen'dar Village, the winged vuldren terror is highly dangerous and should be approached with caution.\nDeliver the beast's head to Danarii Bellowveil to receive your reward.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHunter's Simple Cloak Highlands Defender's Shield\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 775\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"I'll need the creature's head as proof of the deed.","done":"If we didn't have enough on our plates between the cult and the highlands bandits, we don't need a giant vuldren terrorizing our citizens as well. You've done a great thing here today. As promised, here is your reward.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.4,"y":45.8,"n":"Bounty Available: Vulgara the Insatiable!","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.2,"y":45.2,"n":"Danarii Bellowveil","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93958":{"id":93958,"t":"The inner sanctum","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Valennia Stormfist inside the inner sanctum at the Shrine of Akir.","desc":"Valennia's forces just breached the inner sanctum. The fighting was thick in there at first, but it's grown... unsettlingly quiet. Go in there and do your best to link up with Valennia and her forces... if any of them are left.\nI'll stay here and watch your back.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","done":"<Valennia looks gravely wounded.>","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":63.8,"y":50.4,"n":"Hyusaa Quickbreeze","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":65.2,"y":50.4,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8118":{"id":8118,"t":"Vision of Voodress","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Vision of Voodress","rew":"You will receive:\nVision of Voodress\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Sha-mon! Maywiki make a joke!\n<Maywiki laughs.>\nSo, you been using the spirits and elements against our enemies in Zul'Gurub, eh? Spirits be praised!\nMaywiki gonna brighten your orb. Give it here, ‹name›.","done":"Take a look at it now, ‹name›. Voodress come in even clearer now, yea? Let the primal power flow through you, mon.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});